nson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Morrone-Strupinsky</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Reiman</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Network analysis of single-subject fMRI during a finger opposition task.</article-title><source>Neuroimage</source><volume>32(1)</volume><fpage>325</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16733091</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003831-Alexander1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alexander</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name><name><surname>Moeller</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Application of the subprofile model to functional imaging in neuropsychiatric disorders: a principal component approach to modeling brain function in disease.</article-title><source>Hum Brain Mapp</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>79</fpage><lpage>94</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003831-Salmaso1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Salmaso</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Longoni</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1985</year><article-title>Problems in the assessment of hand preference.</article-title><source>Cortex</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>533</fpage><lpage>549</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4092483</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003831-Weder1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weder</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Nienhusmeier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Keel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Leenders</surname><given